                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_235">Guisborough, Yorkshire.
                        Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Provenance inferred
                        from note of s. xvii in Oxford, Bodl. Library, Lat. Misc. c.52, fol. 216r: a
                        copy of the Vitae Abbatum in a hand of s. xvii in Lat. Misc. c.52, fols.
                        216r--231v is stated to be "ex MS. codice monachorum Dunelmensium qui nunc
                        habetur in Bibliotheca D. Augustino Linselli collato cum altero monasterii
                        S. Mariæ de Gisseburn in Bibliotheca Cottoniana". The Cotton MS. can only be
                        Vit. E.i, now partly burnt. </p><p>Vit. E.vii, fols. 1, 2, is a misplaced
                        fragment of Vit. E.i. Five small fragments are kept as Cotton Misc. Burnt
                        Fragments, Bundle I (12).</p></provenance>
